Class vs Object :
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Class : 
A class is a blueprint or template or prototype to  create objects 
Example
class Car {
    String color;
    void drive() {
        System.out.println("Car is driving");
    }
}
Here, Car is a class. It defines what a car object can have and do.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Object :
Object is an instance of a class which denotes the state and behaviour 
Example
Car car1 = new Car();
Car car2 = new Car();
Here, car1 and car2 are objects (instances) of the Car class.
